Make a class `Pelacak` (tracker) that reports every event of its life. Attributes: `static int dibuat`, `int id`, `int nilai` (value). Every new object — copies too — gets the next `id` (1, 2, 3, …).

- the constructor `Pelacak(int v)` prints `+<id>`;
- the copy constructor prints `+<id> salin <id of the source>` and copies `nilai`;
- the assignment operator copies `nilai` only (the id stays) and prints `<id> = <id of the source>`;
- the destructor prints `-<id>`.

The objects are kept in order in a list (an array of pointers); **positions** are counted from 1. Commands:

- `buat v` — a new object with `new`, at the end of the list;
- `salin k` — a new object made by **copying** the object at position k, at the end of the list;
- `tugas a b` — the object at position a `=` the object at position b;
